{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sourish-infinite-tragopan","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Evidence — reproduced, not inferred\n\n`fetcher._iter_pages` (the pager behind `fetcher.collect`, which builds the INBOUND SNAPSHOT the\nentire inbound differ runs on) terminates on a SHORT page and advances by the REQUESTED page size:\n\n    src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py:324-326\n        if len(page) < page_size:\n            return\n        start_at += page_size\n\nJira Data Center silently truncates `maxResults` when it exceeds `jira.search.views.default.max` — a\ncommon hardening, and the same server behaviour already established for this codebase when the\nidentical defect was fixed in `get_parent_map` (change 1105). A truncated FIRST page therefore reads\nas \"that is all there is\".\n\nMeasured against a client that serves 250 issues but caps every page at 20 (default `page_size=100`):\n\n    issues recovered: 20 of 250\n    CONFIRMED DEFECT: 230 issues (92%) silently lost from the inbound snapshot\n\n## Why this is more serious than its two siblings\n\nThis is the THIRD instance of one defect class. The first was `get_parent_map` (fixed, change 1105).\nThe second is [rebar:9263-b404-cb6c-463f] — `get_issuelinks_map` / `get_comment_map`, which lose links\nand comments. This one loses THE ISSUES THEMSELVES.\n\n`collect()` feeds `_build_snapshot`, so a truncated read is not a missing attribute on a present\nissue — it is an issue the pass never sees at all. Every unseen bound issue is a candidate for the\nabsence/deletion path, and every unseen unbound issue simply fails to reconcile. A run in that state\nreports success: it raises nothing, and \"converged\" is true of the 8% it looked at.\n\n## Blast radius — wider than the DC adapter, which is why this is NOT folded into 9263\n\n9263 is confined to `adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py`. This is CORE `fetcher.py`, on the shared\ninbound path, so a change here reaches the live Cloud bridge as well as DC. That is a different risk\nprofile and deserves its own review and its own live verification rather than riding along on an\nadapter-local fix.\n\nCloud reaches the same lines but is not known to be affected in practice: its ceiling and\n`same-token-twice` cursor-stall guards target a different truncation mode, and no short-page\ntruncation has been observed there. The fix must therefore be verified as SAFE FOR CLOUD, not merely\ncorrect for DC.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdvance by `len(page)` and terminate only on an EMPTY page — the same correction already applied to\n`get_parent_map`, whose docstring records the reasoning.\n\nOne thing the `get_parent_map` fix did not have to handle and this one does: `_iter_pages` must not\nspin forever if a server ignores `startAt` and returns the same non-empty page indefinitely. The\nexisting `same-token-twice` guard covers the Cloud CURSOR stall, not an OFFSET stall. Add an\noffset-stall guard that raises `SilentTruncationError` (the type this function already raises for\ntruncation it refuses to hide) rather than looping.\n\n`cap` and ceiling semantics are unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py` — the pager's advance/terminate conditions, plus the\n  offset-stall guard.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` — held-out regression tests.\n\n## Testing\n\n- a client serving N issues while capping every page below the requested size yields ALL N (the\n  reproduction above, which currently returns 20 of 250)\n- an exactly-full final page followed by an empty page terminates without an extra spurious request\n- a server that ignores `startAt` raises `SilentTruncationError` rather than looping forever\n- `cap` still clips, and the ACLI ceiling still raises — asserted so the Cloud contract is pinned\n  unchanged by this fix\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] the 250-issue/20-cap reproduction recovers 250, asserted by a held-out unit test that FAILS on\n      the current code\n- [ ] termination is on an EMPTY page only, and the advance is by `len(page)` — read from the source\n- [ ] a `startAt`-ignoring server raises `SilentTruncationError` instead of looping, asserted by test\n      with a bounded-time guarantee\n- [ ] the existing `cap`, ACLI-ceiling and `same-token-twice` behaviours are unchanged, each asserted\n      by a test that exercises them — this touches the shared Cloud path, so \"DC is fixed\" is not\n      sufficient evidence\n- [ ] the full unit suite passes, and the live DC harness job stays green","id":"deac-4f5a-856a-49bd","parent_id":"e369-a449-4773-48fb","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"fetcher._iter_pages truncates the inbound snapshot on a short page: 92% of issues silently lost"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785518013014435001,"uuid":"b9b2bb22-947b-42a0-8a6d-ff58681bde9e"}